<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Bec de Corbin</h1>
<p>Average Length: Approx. 3 to 5'
Type of Weapon: Close Hand-to-hand.
Commonly used by: Knights and Nobles
</p><p>At first glance, a bec de corbin might be mistaken for a Lucerne hammer, but important functional differences can be noted. The bec de corbin was used late in the Middle Ages by knights and nobles, not by commoners. Its heavy, crows-beak blade was designed to puncture the heavy plate armor common to upper-class warriors. In this weapon the beak is the major feature. This is backed by a flat hammer head, or by a clawed head somewhat similar to that of a Lucerne hammer, and the end spike is more blade like and far shorter than the awl spike of the Lucerne hammer, for the latter weapon was not so specialized.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla there is no bec de corbin skill of its own: such a weapon is fought with the skill of the kind of weapon it is. Look at it to see which (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>).
</p><p><br />
